<title>BRAZIL: Brazil first quarter soybean exports up 31.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Brazil first quarter soybean exports up 31.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exports of Brazilian soybeans rose 31.9 percent in the first quarter compared with the same period last year, inspection company SGS do Brasil said.</p>
<p>Soybean shipments were 769,400 tonnes between January and March, compared with 583,200 tonnes in the same period last year. Shipments of soyoil rose 20.2 percent to 145,200 tonnes, but soymeal exports fell 32.9 percent to 1.28 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Soybeans exports were 725,900 tonnes in March versus 43,500 tonnes in February.</p>
<p>Paranagua port remained the main soy shipper with 715,400 tonnes soybeans, 744,500 tonnes soymeal and 79,400 tonnes soyoil shipped in the first quarter.</p>
<p>Sao Francisco do Sul ranked second with 270,300 tonnes soymeal, followed by Rio Grande with 157,600 tonnes soymeal and 65,800 tonnes soyoil.</p>
<p>Exports, in thousands of tonnes, were as follows:</p>
<p> Product		    Mar 1997     Feb 1997</p>
<p> Soybeans		    725.9	   43.5</p>
<p> Corn			  169.6	   94.6</p>
<p> Corn meal		    40.5	   28.8</p>
<p> Citrus meal		  48.6	   35.4</p>
<p> Soymeal		     978.9	  305.4</p>
<p> Soyoil			107.2	   38.0</p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417))</p>
